# Design charter (visual UI)

## Mandatory application

Any implementation that touches **visual UI** — widgets, layouts, colors, typography, spacing, radius, elevation, icons, motion, dialogs, sheets, empty states, theming — **must** follow [`DESIGN_CHARTER.md`](../../DESIGN_CHARTER.md).

Before coding or changing such UI, read the relevant sections of the charter (tokens, component specs, typography, iconography).

Map values through existing Flutter theme APIs (`Theme.of(context).colorScheme`, `context.planerzColors`, `AppTheme`) as documented in the charter; do not invent parallel one-off styles.

## Precedence over handoffs

Claude Design handoff packages (HTML/React ZIPs) are **reference prototypes**, not a second source of truth.

When a handoff disagrees with the charter — including **future** handoff packages — **`DESIGN_CHARTER.md` wins**.

Resolved cross-package deltas and final arbitrations live in [`DESIGN_CHARTER_INCOHERENCES.md`](../../DESIGN_CHARTER_INCOHERENCES.md). If a new handoff reintroduces an old inconsistency, apply the charter (and the incoherences doc if still listed); do not copy the handoff value blindly.

Handoffs remain useful for **layout, copy, and interaction flow**; visual tokens and component rules come from the charter.
